# Education Operations Rules

- Core entities: courses, classes, sessions, students, parents, teachers, attendance, makeup credits, reports, payroll.
- Class schedules are generated from start date, fixed weekdays, time slots, total sessions, room, and teacher.
- Vietnam holidays must be configurable. Default behavior: skip holiday sessions and propose/auto-create makeup sessions based on the same weekday/slot when configured.
- Attendance states must distinguish present, absent with permission, absent without permission, and note/review when supported.
- Absence with permission may create makeup eligibility, but exact makeup rules must remain configurable.
- Teacher payroll should support taught sessions, teaching hours, and manual approval before finalization.
- End-of-course reports should support PDF for parents, Excel for internal use, dashboard view, and AI-generated comments based on actual data.
- Do not hardcode business policies that the user said are still unclear; design them as configurable domain rules.
